WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.482
Data quality has multiple dimensions.

00:00:02.482 --> 00:00:05.302
Completeness is not the same as validity.

00:00:05.302 --> 00:00:08.177
Validity is not the same as uniqueness.

00:00:08.177 --> 00:00:11.232
Timeliness asks a different question again.

00:00:11.232 --> 00:00:14.722
Measure these dimensions separately whenever possible.

00:00:14.722 --> 00:00:21.627
A single score can be useful for triage, but it can hide which problem actually caused the low

00:00:21.627 --> 00:00:26.582
score. Validation is rule-based detection, not automatic correction.

00:00:26.582 --> 00:00:30.947
A failed email-shape check tells you that a record deserves attention;

00:00:30.947 --> 00:00:33.537
it does not tell you the correct email.

00:00:33.537 --> 00:00:40.640
Treat quality flags as evidence that can drive quarantine, review, or a documented repair process.
